            "body": "@devOgazi has applied to work on this issue as part of the **Stellar Wave Program**'s 11th wave.\n\n<!-- wave:application-id:d578f932-7424-433e-8ede-57c74d7bc8a7 -->\n<!-- wave:app-text-start -->\n> I\u2019d like to work on this issue because dispute and refund timing is a security-critical part of a payment channel, and relying solely on a provider-declared manifest creates a trust gap between advertised and actual on-chain behavior. Verifying the deployed channel contract configuration before opening a session provides stronger guarantees and helps prevent users from interacting with channels that could lock refunds for unsafe or unexpected periods.\n> \n> I have experience working with TypeScript SDKs, blockchain integrations, on-chain state verification, and security-focused validation. I\u2019m comfortable reusing existing contract simulation and state-reading infrastructure, validating the deployed channel's configuration against the provider manifest, enforcing sensible upper bounds, and raising clear errors when inconsistencies are detected. I\u2019ll also update the dispute-resolution documentation and add appropriate tests covering matching values, mismatches, and excessive waiting periods.\n<!-- wave:app-text-end -->\n\n\u2139\ufe0f **Repo Maintainers**: To accept this application, [review their application](https://www.drips.network/wave/maintainers/issues/358b38bf-5353-47fb-938d-356dca56761c) or assign @devOgazi to this issue.",
